  "semantic_review_scope": "Final scope review by atlas_semantics plus independent second scope-only pass by atlas_audit; root separately read all 21 scopes and required explicit Curry–Howard fragment matching. Shared model/context, not independent human peer review.",
  "critical_scope_review": [
    "001: Wiles is scoped to semistable elliptic curves over Q, not all number fields.",
    "002: Viazovska is dimension 8 and all sphere packings, not merely lattices.",
    "003: AHK uses a finite nonempty loopless matroid and an ample class; representability is not required.",
    "004: Moser–Tardos requires finite independent variables and finite bad events with the displayed local-lemma criterion.",
    "005: Green–Tao uses a pseudorandom/transference setup; primality is not positive density among all integers.",
    "006: Lott–Villani recorded scope is compact measured length spaces and existence of an appropriate Wasserstein geodesic.",
    "007: Expander-code guarantee explicitly remains conditional on the selected quantitative expansion/local-code construction; no universal expander guarantee.",
    "008: Stable regularity uses fixed non-k-order property in model theory; endpoint is not dynamical stability.",
    "009: Base Curry–Howard correspondence is intuitionistic implication versus function-only simply typed lambda calculus; conjunction/disjunction/false require matching product/sum/empty types and rules. Unrestricted recursion is not treated as proof.",
    "010: HoTT adds explicit identity-type/univalence assumptions, not an automatic property of all type theories.",
    "011: Jones construction is for tame oriented links and a Markov-compatible trace; not a complete knot invariant.",
    "012: Covering classification retains path connectivity, local path connectivity and semilocal simple connectivity; unpointed classification uses conjugacy classes.",
    "013: Algebraic-set/radical-ideal correspondence assumes algebraically closed base field and finite-variable polynomial ring.",
    "014: Gauss–Bonnet is an invariant_identity, not object-level equivalence; recorded scope is compact oriented boundaryless regular surfaces in R^3.",
    "015: Feynman–Kac recorded sufficient scope has bounded smooth nonnegative potential and bounded smooth initial data; generator is half-Laplacian.",
    "016: CRT source version uses delta_3S+3delta_4S<2, bounded noise and a global l1 minimizer.",
    "017: JL keeps n>=2, 0<epsilon<1 and positive integer target dimension; exact embedding covers target dimension above original dimension.",
    "018: Guth keeps finite bounded-complexity varieties, D>=1 and only complementary cells outside the zero set.",
    "019: Theta gives a bound for finite simple graphs and strong products; equality is claimed only for C5.",
    "020: Reed–Solomon uses distinct finite-field evaluation points and degree<k; erasure recovery is separate from unknown-error correction.",
    "021: Sum-check keeps degree checking, fresh uniform challenges and trusted final polynomial evaluation; soundness is min(1,md/|F|)."
  ],
